Collection Framework is a collection of classes and interface which have ability to work
on data which store more than single value in our java objects every instance is created to store
more single value we have three major interface for every Collections in Java class.

Generic Datatypes(every datatype will store it's class data)
1)int ->Integer
2)float ->Float
3)String->String
4)boolean->Boolean

Note:All this collections are stored in java.util.*;

1)List:It is mutable(means we can add ,update ,delete ,sort ,index ) collection of data.list enclosed in square
bracket [].List interface have two major class to perform ArrayList,LinkedList

1)ArrayList is used to store data normally like a array in java which hold index from 0 to n-1,
syntax:

ArrayList <Datatype> object=new ArrayList<>();


1)LinkedList It store data in node form where each connected with it's adjacent node in array so
we can easily find distance or difference between two nodes in LinkedList
syntax:

LinkedList <Datatype> object=new LinkedList<>();


Note:list is used to store different data in different location and it also allow duplicate entries.

2)Set:It is used to store data with unique values means if one set already have that value it not allow
duplicate entry.It enclosed data in curly bracket.Set is unordered collection.


Types of Set interface class:
1)HashSet:It is used to store particular data is hash format so Every element will appear only once in
given pair.
syntax:
    HashSet<Datatype>object=new HashSet<>();


3)Map:It is used to store data in key-value pair in Map.means In this we call data using it's key
not index.It enclosed in curly bracket {key:value}
syntax:
HashMap<Datatype,Datatype>object=new HashMap<>();


